invariant: INV-17
file: gcm_avx512.c
catches: test/avx512-run.sh bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test
builds: bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test
reason: gcm_open_avx512 returns without calling avx512_wipe_registers, so
  the round keys, the keystream, H, E(K, J0) and the GHASH sums the kernel
  ran through the 512-bit registers stay there after the call. Every byte
  it writes is still right. bin/gcm_avx512_equiv_test stores zmm0 to zmm31
  and k1 to k7 after each entry's call and requires them zero. It needs a
  CPU with what CH_CPU_AVX512 names, or Intel SDE through SDE64, which the
  nightly's test-invariants job installs; without either this reports
  unguarded rather than caught.

--- old
    wipe_frame_call();
    avx512_wipe_registers();
}

#endif
--- new
    wipe_frame_call();
}

#endif
